    "attributes": {
        "action": "Reduce the minimum school week to 31 hours and 15 minutes",
        "additional_details": "We believe children may work harder if they have a reward and that shorter school weeks could make adults and children happier and improve productivity. We think this could improve the quality of work and test results. It could also help the economy because people could go out earlier and spend more money.",
        "background": "Reduce the minimum expected length of the school week in England from 32.5 hours to 31 hours and 15 minutes.",
